# minimal_defconfig — smallest buildable configuration: the hard-required
# core (folly, Boost, HTTP transport plain-HTTP) stays enabled since it is
# outside Kconfig's control entirely (find_package(folly)/find_package(Boost)
# run unconditionally regardless of any CONFIG symbol — see cmake/Kconfig.cmake
# and the design doc's "Kconfig expresses intent; CMake still does detection"
# principle), and every genuinely optional feature is explicitly off,
# including HTTPS/TLS support for the HTTP transport itself.
# CONFIG_OPENSSL and CONFIG_HTTP_TRANSPORT are left at their Kconfig default
# (y) rather than forced off: OpenSSL is needed by certificate_authority
# regardless, and disabling the HTTP transport target entirely isn't a
# configuration this project's CMakeLists.txt supports switching off (only
# its TLS layer, CONFIG_HTTP_TRANSPORT_TLS, is genuinely optional).
# CONFIG_HTTP_TRANSPORT_TLS is not set
# CONFIG_COAP_TRANSPORT is not set
# CONFIG_DNS_DISCOVERY is not set
# CONFIG_POCO_DISCOVERY is not set
# CONFIG_AWS_SDK is not set
# CONFIG_LIBSSH2_TESTS is not set
# CONFIG_CHAOS_TESTS is not set
